## DEFINITION
Verify3D is a protein structure validation tool that evaluates the compatibility of a 3D protein model with its amino acid sequence.

## PURPOSE
- Validate 3D protein structures.
- Assess sequence–structure compatibility.
- Identify poorly modeled regions.
- Improve confidence in predicted structures.

## APPLICATIONS
- Protein structure validation.
- Quality assessment of predicted models.
- Comparison of refined protein structures.
- Structural biology and bioinformatics research.

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- PDB (.pdb) protein structure file.

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Evaluates each residue based on its 3D environment.
- Reports the percentage of residues with acceptable scores.
- Commonly used with ERRAT and PROCHECK for comprehensive validation.
- Higher Verify3D scores indicate better model quality.
